# os-local ignore for x86_64 build artifacts (P1-030). Kept under os/ (NOT the repo root) so the rule
# lives next to the thing it governs and the diff stays within os/. It is OUTSIDE the ts-overlay tree
# on purpose: mkosi copies the overlay into the rootfs via `--extra-tree=os/x86_64/ts-overlay`, so a
# .gitignore inside that tree would be shipped into the image as /.gitignore. Placing it one level up
# keeps dev/build-only files out of the image while still ignoring the artifact.
#
# The Deno runtime binary is a BUILD ARTIFACT, not source: os/x86_64/ts-image.mjs fetches the
# version- + sha256-pinned upstream zip, verifies it, and stages the single `deno` executable at
# ts-overlay/usr/lib/vita/deno before mkosi runs `--extra-tree`. It is large and reproducible from the
# pin, so it is never committed. The committed TS sources under ts-overlay/usr/lib/vita/ts/ (main.ts +
# vendor/*) and the systemd unit + wants-symlink stay tracked — the path below anchors to the FILE.
ts-overlay/usr/lib/vita/deno

# Vita LUKS TEST keystore. THROWAWAY, per-host, generated by tools/luks-test-keys.sh,
# and never part of a reproducible or shipped image.
.luks/

# Vita mesh TEST WireGuard keystore. THROWAWAY, per-host, generated for boot/test
# proofs only; real owner-held mesh private keys are never committed.
.mesh/
